WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.534
-Well, the rolling GOP meltdown

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.567
that began with the party's
humiliating speaker vote

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.534
keeps getting crazier.
Two members of Congress,

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:09.200
Lauren Boebert
and Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.601
reportedly got into a shouting
match in a bathroom;

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.634
serial liar George Santos

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:16.367
is facing calls
from his own party to resign;

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.000
and, just in time
to cool things down,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.968
Donald Trump
is reportedly getting ready

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.667
to rejoin Facebook and Twitter.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.734
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.868
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:27.734
♪♪
[ Whistling ]

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:28.934
Back in November,

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:31.067
Republicans delivered one
of the worst performances

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.267
for an opposition party
in decades

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.067
and, after the results came in,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.567
they all started turning
on each other

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.634
and, surprisingly,
on Donald Trump.

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:40.367
-Donald Trump kept saying,

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:41.567
"We're going to be
winning so much,

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.734
we'll get tired of winning."

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:43.801
I'm tired of losing.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:44.767
I mean, that's all he's done.

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:45.834
-Look, I don't think

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.968
he can win in November of '24.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.467
-Trump is the past.

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.567
-He's fading fast.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:51.701
He's a proven loser.

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.234
He cost us the House in '18.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.534
He cost us
the White House in '20.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.968
He cost us the Senate
again and again.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.067
And I think we all know that

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.634
and I think
we're moving past Trump.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.567
-First of all, it should be easy
to move past Trump,

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:03.367
since he moves
at the speed of a glacier

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.434
smoking pot in a windstorm.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.467
Remember when he used to lumber

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.467
around the debate stage

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Laughter ]
like a zombie who forgot

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.200
what he was supposed
to be doing?

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.701
[ As Trump ]
I was just in the middle
of something.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.434
[ Laughter ]
What -- Oh, right.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.434
Eat brains!

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:22.334
[ Laughter ]
Even when he was the president
of the United States

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:24.334
and he actually
had important places to be,

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.601
he'd just wander
slowly in circles,
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:30.467
like a guy with a metal detector
on the beach

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.133
who then lost
the metal detector.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.868
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ] This is why --

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:37.234
This is why you need
the second metal detector.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:39.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:40.934
The metal detector detector.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.067
Trump is, somehow,
both extremely slow

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.067
and also incapable
of standing still.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.701
At least, when Joe Biden finds
himself wandering aimlessly,

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:50.100
he freezes in place...

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.834
...trying to figure out what he
was supposed to be doing.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:57.501
He just freezes like a possum

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:00.234
that turned on the motion
sensor lights in your driveway.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:03.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:06.834
"You guys, uh,
move the garbage cans?"

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:08.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.467
Alright, well, let's see here.

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.567
We're just starting
our "Closer Look" and that's --

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.634
Let's see,
that's Trump at the debate,

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.133
that's Trump wandering
on the lawn,

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.100
and that's Biden freezing
on the stage.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.467
And, as we call it here,
at "Late Night,"

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:18.934
triple classic vids!

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.300
[ Electronic voice ]

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.634
[ Vuvuzela blasting ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:26.067
[ Air guitar sting ]

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:28.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.601
Also, it's nice that Republicans
finally learned how

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:36.434
to hurt Trump's feelings --
just call him a proven loser.

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.634
It's one thing to call him
a loser. Anyone can do that.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.367
But proven loser
is a nice turn of phrase.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.234
It's like something they'd put
on a bottle

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.067
of Trump-branded diet pills.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.501
That said, the last person
I want to hear from right now

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.133
is this guy, Paul Ryan.
You guys remember him,

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.801
the guy who looks like
if Eddie Munster worked

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.634
at the Heritage Foundation.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:54.868
He was speaker of the House

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.601
for the first two years
of Trump's presidency

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.501
and happily joined forces
with Trump

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.234
whenever it was convenient
for the GOP.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:03.400
Sorry, you just don't get
to dump Trump now, you know.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.801
That's just easy for you now.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:08.334
That's like taking Tom Brady
off your fantasy team this week.

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:09.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.501
You're not brave, dude.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.100
So, Republicans
are turning on Trump

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.601
and declaring, unequivocally,
that Trump is in the past,

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.467
which means it's
the perfect time for Trump

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.767
to come back
to Facebook and Twitter.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.667
-Mounting a comeback
for the White House,

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.567
former President Donald Trump
is preparing a return

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.801
to his Facebook
and Twitter accounts.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.100
With access to his Twitter
account restored,

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.434
Trump's campaign
is formally petitioning

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:35.167
Facebook's parent company
to unblock his account there

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.601
after it was locked in response

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.000
to the U.S. Capitol riot
two years ago.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.267
-Trump's team is reportedly
planning his return to Twitter

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:45.434
and even workshopping what his
first tweet will be.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.367
[ Laughter ]
-That's right,
Trump's staff is supposedly

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:49.868
workshopping ideas
for his first tweet.

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:52.234
Did you guys forget
how his tweets work?

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:55.501
No matter how insane, they were
immediately lost to history

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.200
when he wrote his next tweet.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.367
[ Laughter ]
"This tweet is the craziest
[bleep] I've ever read!

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.701
Hold up. This new tweet is
the craziest [bleep]

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:04.334
[ Laughter ]
I've ever read!
Hold up."

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.200
But I think it's great
that Trump's team

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.367
is sitting around workshopping
ideas for his first tweet.

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:09.968
I hope they're really
burning the midnight oil

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:11.901
and taking weeks
to craft the perfect message

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:14.133
that will appeal to voters
across the political spectrum,

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.767
do extensive market research,

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:18.033
test it with audiences,
rewrite it, proofread it,

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:20.200
[ Laughter ]
and then present it to Trump,
just so he can say --

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.968
[ As Trump ]
This is great, fellas,
but I'm going to go with...

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:27.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.400
It's so -- It's so sad, they had
to put a second "D" on it.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.534
Now, if this is true,
the timing of Trump's return

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:35.934
cannot be worse for the GOP,

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.968
given that they're already
at each other's throats,

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.834
and Trump forcing himself
back into the spotlight

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:40.968
will only make it worse.

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:42.901
Trump is not who you bring in

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.534
to de-escalate the situation.

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:47.467
He would be a terrible
hostage negotiator.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.567
[ As Trump ]
I don't think you have
the guts to kill them.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:50.634
Let go.

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:51.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:52.968
It's my bullhorn now.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:54.234
You guys brought me in.

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:57.367
GOP infighting
has gotten so bad,

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:59.734
even one-time allies are now
bitter enemies,

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.501
like Lauren Boebert
and Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.767
who were once friends,

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:05.334
but were on opposite sides
of the speaker fight.

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:06.667
Boebert and Greene
reportedly got

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.734
into a heated argument
in the bathroom at the Capitol

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:12.234
while all of the drama of the
speaker vote was going down.

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.200
-New details of a bathroom brawl

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.567
in the middle
of the speaker fight.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:18.234
According to The Daily Beast,
Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.067
once a staunch critic
of the Republican leadership,

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:23.133
was in a near fight in the
middle of the marathon vote.

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:25.267
Greene reportedly screaming
at her colleague

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:27.000
and former friend
Lauren Boebert,

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.133
a McCarthy holdout,

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:30.400
in a bathroom
right off the House floor.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.634
-Well, I guess
that answers the riddle

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:32.868
'What's worse
than Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:34.167
and Lauren Boebert fighting?'

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.868
Marjorie Taylor Greene
and Lauren Boebert fighting

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.033
in a room with an echo.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.267
[ As Greene ]
Do you know who I am?!

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:40.434
Am?! Am?! Am?! Am?! Am?!

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:41.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.200
Marjorie Taylor Greene
does strike me

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.234
as the kind of person who would
wait in a bathroom stall

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:47.400
until she overheard someone
talking [bleep] about her,

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.067
then just kick open the door

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:51.234
like a cowboy busting
into a saloon.

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:53.434
[ Laughter ]
[ As Greene ]
Oh, you think I'm a lot?

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.167
So, that's where
we're at right now.

00:05:57.167 --> 00:06:00.334
The GOP is embroiled in a messy
and very public civil war

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:01.367
and, to make matters worse,

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:02.901
they also have to deal
with the fallout

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:05.033
from a truly
head-spinning scandal

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:07.501
involving yet another one
of their disgraced members,

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:10.167
a guy supposedly named
George Santos,

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.901
[ Laughter ]
who was just elected

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:13.934
from New York's 3rd District
on Long Island.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:17.167
As you may have heard,
Santos is a serial liar

00:06:17.167 --> 00:06:18.300
who's been caught fabricating

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.300
virtually every detail
of his life story.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:21.634
Every day we learn

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:23.267
that something else about him
was a lie

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:27.067
and now, he's facing growing
calls from almost everyone,

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.968
on all sides of the political
spectrum, to step down.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:31.667
-It seems like every day we're
learning something else

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:34.868
about George Santos' life
that simply isn't true.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.767
Now, he's being accused
of stealing funds

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:39.000
from a homeless veteran's
dying dog

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.834
and lying about his mother
being a 9/11 survivor.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.067
-Santos has admitted to...

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:47.467
and to...

00:06:47.467 --> 00:06:50.100
-There's a staggering amount
of fantastical tales

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:52.167
George Santos has told
over the years.

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:54.534
Saying he caught a severe
early case of COVID,

00:06:54.534 --> 00:06:56.701
even though he was on TV
four days later.

00:06:56.701 --> 00:06:59.534
Claiming to be
a "proud American Jew"

00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:02.000
whose parents fled Hitler,

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.133
even though
he's actually Catholic

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:05.267
[ Laughter ]
and has no Jewish ancestors,

00:07:05.267 --> 00:07:07.534
as far as we can tell
from the records.

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:09.434
Said he owned
13 different properties,

00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:11.000
when he's never
been a landlord.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.033
-This is the same George Santos
who said he worked

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.734
at Goldman Sachs,
which was a lie;

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:16.467
who said he worked at Citigroup,
which he didn't,

00:07:16.467 --> 00:07:18.267
meaning that, too, was a lie.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:19.567
It's the same George Santos
who lied

00:07:19.567 --> 00:07:21.334
about the high school
he went to in New York

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:23.100
and the college he said
he graduated from.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.300
He said it was Baruch College
and he got a degree

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.167
in economics and finance.
He didn't.

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:40.267
Also allegedly stolen by George,
according to these two men,

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:41.767
this Burberry scarf

00:07:41.767 --> 00:07:42.901
[ Laughter and applause ]
that George wore

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:45.200
to a pro-Trump rally
in Washington, D.C.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.701
-More questions are being raised

00:07:46.701 --> 00:07:49.434
about New York
Congressman George Santos,

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:52.067
including if that's even
his real name.

00:07:52.067 --> 00:07:53.300
[ Laughter ]
An ex-roommate

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.534
of the freshman congressman
had this to say --

00:07:56.534 --> 00:07:58.734
-I've always known him
as Anthony Devolder.

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:01.601
[ Laughter ]
I've never known him
as George Santos.

00:08:01.601 --> 00:08:03.667
[ Laughter ]
-That's right, George Santos
lied about so many things,

00:08:03.667 --> 00:08:05.601
we don't even know if his
real name is George Santos,

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:07.267
which, in a way,
is not surprising.

00:08:07.267 --> 00:08:09.400
I mean, just look at him.
He looks like he's wearing

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.634
a crappy disguise
from "The Americans."

00:08:11.634 --> 00:08:12.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.868 --> 00:08:14.934
His lies have been
so numerous and fantastical,

00:08:14.934 --> 00:08:16.267
it's impossible to keep track.

00:08:16.267 --> 00:08:19.701
He even lied about being
a college volleyball star,

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:22.400
[ Laughter ]
which the chair of the
Nassau County Republican Party

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.934
revealed in a press conference
last week,

00:08:24.934 --> 00:08:26.901
where he called
on Santos to resign,

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:29.701
causing the other Republicans
assembled behind him

00:08:29.701 --> 00:08:31.501
to laugh at how absurd it was.

00:08:31.501 --> 00:08:33.367
-Told me,
I remember specifically --

00:08:33.367 --> 00:08:35.000
I'm into sports a little bit --

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.367
that he was a star
on the volleyball team

00:08:37.367 --> 00:08:39.968
and that they won
the league championship.

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:40.801
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.801 --> 00:08:42.634
What can I tell ya?

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:44.067
-You got to love
New York politics.

00:08:44.067 --> 00:08:46.567
Even our leaders address
damning scandals

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:48.367
like they're doing
a one-man show at Carolines.

00:08:48.367 --> 00:08:50.033
[ Laughter ]
[ Italian accent ] He told me
his mother was Italian,

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:52.667
his father was Jewish,
and he was in therapy.

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:53.968
What can I tell ya?

00:08:53.968 --> 00:08:56.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.601
That's how ridiculous
this scandal is.

00:08:57.601 --> 00:09:00.100
Even they can't help but laugh,
and how can you not?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.434
Claiming you're a star
volleyball player,

00:09:03.434 --> 00:09:06.033
[ Laughter ]
at Baruch College, no less?

00:09:06.033 --> 00:09:07.734
[ Laughter ]
A public college
in New York City,

00:09:07.734 --> 00:09:09.968
not exactly renowned
for its volleyball program.

00:09:09.968 --> 00:09:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.801 --> 00:09:12.234
It's a pretty incredible lie.

00:09:12.234 --> 00:09:15.834
Like I don't even see how that
lie is designed to help you.

00:09:15.834 --> 00:09:17.868
"We need a candidate
to run in the 3rd District."

00:09:17.868 --> 00:09:19.133
[ New York accent ]
I got just the guy.

00:09:19.133 --> 00:09:20.234
Baruch College,

00:09:20.234 --> 00:09:21.934
volleyball star.

00:09:21.934 --> 00:09:23.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.567
Can't lose!

00:09:24.567 --> 00:09:26.567
[ Laughter ]
Also, I'm pretty sure

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:28.667
